{"_id":"68a7361e8ec3d8323af1808a","nodeId":"p5u2tWRmRtyfBgKcSUHFU","roadmapSlug":"golang","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:09.800Z","description":"# Deadlines & Cancellations\n\nContext package mechanisms for controlling operation lifetime and propagating cancellation signals. Supports deadlines (absolute time) or timeouts (duration). Functions should check `ctx.Done()` and return early when cancelled. Essential for robust concurrent applications.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Canceling in-progress Operations","url":"https://go.dev/doc/database/cancel-operations","_id":"6a26767c7e97c9d3f8b8d86c"},{"type":"article","title":"Understanding Golang Context: Cancellation, Timeouts","url":"https://webdevstation.com/posts/understanding-golang-context/","_id":"6a26767c7e97c9d3f8b8d86d"},{"type":"article","title":"Understanding Context in Golang","url":"https://medium.com/better-programming/understanding-context-in-golang-7f574d9d94e0","_id":"6a26767c7e97c9d3f8b8d86e"},{"type":"article","title":"How to use the context.Done() method in Go","url":"https://dev.to/mcaci/how-to-use-the-context-done-method-in-go-22me","_id":"6a26767c7e97c9d3f8b8d86f"}],"updatedAt":"2026-06-08T07:59:56.882Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/golang/content/p5u2tWRmRtyfBgKcSUHFU.md"}